titre$ . KEY TO HYMENOCHAETACEAE
1,2 $ Basidiocarp more or less centrally stipitate, usually on the ground; setae never present 
1,3 $ Basidiocarp resupinate or pileate, sometimes with a lateral, tapering base; setae present or absent 
2,0 $ Basidiocarp usually thin and pliable; gloeocystidia absent in the hymenium; mycorrhizal or causing a white rot $ Coltricia
2,0 $  Basidiocarp large and fleshy, gloeocystidia present in hymenium; causing a brown rot (not belonging in the family)$Phaeolus
3,0 $  Hyphal system dimitic with skeletal hyphae; basidiocarps mostly woody, perennial with layered tubes$Phellinus
3,4 $ Hyphal system monomitic or pred.ominantly so, basidiocarps mostly fragile when dry, annual; species growing on living bushes belong here 
4,0 $ Context distinctly duplex, upper loose part often separated from the lowerdense part by a black zone; setae absent; spores usually abundandy present, ellipsoid, pale yellowish, shorter than 4.5 uum ; on living trees or shrubs $Phylloporia
4,0 $ Context homogeneous; setae present or absent; spores hyaline to rusty brown; longer than 4.5 uum, on dead wood $Inonotus
